---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { baseUrl } from '../../utils/base.ts';
---

<Layout
  title="Roadmap - UOMP"
  description="UOMP protocol and Aegis OS memory module roadmap: native commands, data plane, unified trusted UI, and remote Agents."
  lang="en"
  switchHref={`${baseUrl}roadmap/`}
>
  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Roadmap</h1>
      <p>UOMP is the protocol; Aegis OS is the native implementation.</p>

      <div class="roadmap">
        <div class="note">
          <strong>Current focus:</strong> native commands and the data plane are done; the remaining priority is the unified web trusted UI.
        </div>

        <h2>Done <span class="status status-done">Done</span></h2>
        <ul class="roadmap-list">
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>UOMP-Draft-00 spec and Aegis OS field mapping</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Aegis policy / lease / escalation / trusted approval</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Aegis Memory Gateway: JWT, TLS/mTLS, session check, rate limiting, audit</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Agent write staging and high-sensitivity rejection</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Encrypted payload upload / read / delete</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Remote Agent device flow and one-time remote token</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span><code>aos-memory-store</code>: UOMP-compatible SQLite schema + Markdown importer + staged writes + payloads</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span><code>aos-memory-server</code>: native consent requests, sessions, Ed25519 JWT, revocation, audit</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>Agent-first consent: <code>memory setup</code> does not pre-authorize; the first tool call requests consent</li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span>All native <code>aegis-os memory</code> commands, including <code>serve/setup/pending/approve/deny/audit/connect/disconnect/sessions/revoke</code></li>
          <li><span class="status status-done">Done</span><code>uomp-core</code> / <code>uomp-mvp</code> archived; no Node or reference CLI at runtime</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>In progress <span class="status status-current">In progress</span></h2>
        <ul class="roadmap-list">
          <li><span class="status status-next">Next</span>Unified web trusted UI (UOMP + Aegis)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Later <span class="status status-future">Planned</span></h2>
        <ul class="roadmap-list">
          <li><span class="status status-future">Later</span>CSV / JSON connectors and a <code>~/.uomp</code> migration tool</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Later</span>Aegis Cloud remote Agent auto-configuration</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Later</span>Standalone daemon / sandbox / OS keychain</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Later</span>UOMP conformance suite</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Research <span class="status status-future">Not scheduled</span></h2>
        <ul class="roadmap-list">
          <li><span class="status status-future">Research</span>FHE (homomorphic encryption)</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Research</span>On-chain audit</li>
          <li><span class="status status-future">Research</span>TEE / remote Agent isolation</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Definition of done</h2>
        <div class="metric-grid">
          <div class="metric"><strong>1</strong><span>user installs only Aegis OS</span></div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>0</strong><span>memory commands that need Node</span></div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>1</strong><span>unified trusted UI</span></div>
          <div class="metric"><strong>0</strong><span>same-user Agent direct data access</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>
          The first, second, and fourth are already true; the unified web trusted UI is the remaining item.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-btns" style="margin-top:2.5rem;">
        <a href={`${baseUrl}en/try/`} class="btn-h1">Try via Aegis OS →</a>
        <a href={`${baseUrl}en/spec/`} class="btn-h1">Read the spec →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
